questions.question_text:
The graph of $y=x^{n}$ is shown.
Is $n$ odd or even?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-3.2,0)--(3.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3.2)--(0,3.2) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-1.35:1.35,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.8*\x*\x*\x*\x});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The cubic graph shown has the form $y=k(x-b)^{3}+c$.
Which equation could it be?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-3.2,0)--(3.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3.6)--(0,3.6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-1.6:1.9,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.45*(\x*\x*\x-3)});
\fill (0,-1.35) circle (2pt);
\node[left] at (0,-1.35) {$(0,-3)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
